R12-CICD-9083: commit the running round's lane manifest and require the Agent-Lane trailer
==========================================================================================

Lane L6 (l6-platform) wrote this file. It changes protected paths
(scripts/agent-policy.json, scripts/lanes/**, the guard's tests,
.github/workflows/ci.yml), so it is a patch for the orchestrator to apply.
git apply ignores everything above the first "diff --git" line.

WHAT IT DOES

The owner's ruling of 2026-10-31 on CICD-9083 says: "Require the trailer:
from the instant the running round's manifest is committed, every agent commit
names its lane, and one that names none is refused, the orchestrator's
included." The patch does six things.

1. Adds scripts/lanes/round-wave1031.json, the running round as 39 lanes.
   Each of the eleven sessions (L1, L1b, L2, L2b, L3, L3b, L4, L4b, L5, L5b,
   L6) on branch ccr-d1bc1e54-kf6mr0-<session> is split by role into
   <session>-code (backend-engineer), -tests (test-engineer), -docs
   (technical-writer) and, for L1b and L6, -platform (cloud-platform-engineer).
   Four orchestrator lanes on ccr-116bbb27-osu8n8 (orchestrator-code, -tests,
   -docs, -platform) each depend on all 35 session lanes. Territories come
   from the branches' diffs since 725c180b, read at e1563525. The manifest's
   "comment" says how they were read, how overlaps are ordered (by merge
   order within each role), and which paths no role may edit.
2. Points scripts/agent-policy.json lane_manifest.path at that manifest.
3. Sets lane_manifest.trailer_required_after to the placeholder
   REPLACE-WITH-THE-INSTANT-OF-THE-APPLY-COMMIT, and updates the comment.
4. Updates scripts/agent-guard.test.mjs and scripts/agent-lanes.test.mjs:
   - the round-3 lane tests read round-3.json as a fixture;
   - the role, protection, review and range tests run with the trailer
     off, because their fixture commits name no lane;
   - new tests check the committed switch and the new manifest.
5. Points ci.yml's scripts job validate step at the new manifest.
6. Updates scripts/game-day/agent-escalation.mjs, the agent-authority drill
   (SEC-10157), and its tests in harness.test.mjs.
   - The drill judges the committed policy. With the switch on, its control
     attempt (an unlaned in-role change) would be refused, and every other
     attempt would be refused for the missing lane as well as for its own
     rule. A broken protected-path rule would then read as held.
   - To prevent that, the existing attempts are dated before any switch.
   - A new attempt, "an agent commit naming no lane, made now, after the
     lane-trailer instant", is dated at the drill's instant and must be
     refused.
   - A new harness test proves the drill fails on that attempt alone when
     the switch is off.

THE PLACEHOLDER, AND WHY NOT null

agent-guard.mjs step 1c runs Date.parse on trailer_required_after:
- null turns the gate off with no signal;
- an unparseable string refuses every agent change ("... which is not a
  date");
- any parseable string turns the gate on from that date.

So the patch ships a string that fails loudly instead of a null that fails
silently. The placeholder contains no digits on purpose. An earlier draft
ended in "-ISO-8601-UTC", and Date.parse reads that as 8601-01-01, which
would have turned the gate off until the year 8601. The new guard test
asserts Number.isNaN(Date.parse(placeholder)).

Until the placeholder is replaced, two things fail:
- every agent change is refused;
- "the committed policy turns the lane trailer on" fails, naming the
  placeholder.
That test also refuses null and a future instant.

APPLY ORDER (orchestrator, on ccr-116bbb27-osu8n8)

1. Tell every running session that the trailer is required. Give each
   session its lane ids from the manifest: <session>-code, -tests, -docs,
   -platform. Tell them that a commit names the one lane its files lie in,
   and that a commit spanning two lanes must be split into two commits.
   Commits dated before the instant are not judged, so in-flight work is
   safe. Unlaned commits after the instant are refused.
2. git apply --check docs/blueprint/lanes/l6-cicd-9083-lane-manifest.patch
   git apply docs/blueprint/lanes/l6-cicd-9083-lane-manifest.patch
3. Replace REPLACE-WITH-THE-INSTANT-OF-THE-APPLY-COMMIT in
   scripts/agent-policy.json with the output of
   date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ, taken just before committing. It must not
   be later than the apply commit's own committer date.
4. Run the checks. On e1563525 plus this patch, the instant filled:
   - validate prints 12 waves and exits 0;
   - the three agent suites print "pass 67, fail 0";
   - ci.yml's whole scripts-job list prints "pass 212, fail 0".
   node scripts/agent-lanes.mjs validate --policy scripts/agent-policy.json --manifest scripts/lanes/round-wave1031.json
   node --test scripts/agent-guard.test.mjs scripts/agent-lanes.test.mjs scripts/agent-egress.test.mjs
   node --test scripts/model-gateway.test.mjs scripts/fleet/dispatch.test.mjs scripts/fleet/worker.test.mjs scripts/sast-gate.test.mjs scripts/agent-guard.test.mjs scripts/agent-lanes.test.mjs scripts/agent-egress.test.mjs scripts/game-day/harness.test.mjs scripts/rule-citation.test.mjs
5. Commit with the trailer "Agent-Lane: orchestrator-platform". The apply
   commit is after the instant, so it needs a lane. Every file it changes is
   in that lane's owns:
   - scripts/agent-policy.json
   - scripts/lanes/round-wave1031.json
   - scripts/agent-guard.test.mjs
   - scripts/agent-lanes.test.mjs
   - scripts/game-day/agent-escalation.mjs
   - scripts/game-day/harness.test.mjs
   - .github/workflows/ci.yml
   Then push.

This patch has no ordering dependency on l6-cicd-10203-sha-pins.patch. Both
change ci.yml in hunks that do not touch, and each applies with or without
the other.

BEFORE STEP 3, KNOW THIS

- The rolling integration pull request will be refused.
  - Cause: agent-guard.mjs step 1b, unchanged here, holds the whole pull
    request's file list to every lane its commits name. The pull request
    API gives no per-commit file list.
  - Effect: one pull request carrying two lanes' commits is refused for
    each lane, even when each commit stays inside its own lane.
  - Before this switch, unlaned commits never hit that rule. After it, the
    ccr-116bbb27-osu8n8 -> main pull request will hit it, and a person's
    approval does not clear a 1b refusal.
  - The judgeRange step at deploy judges each commit against its own files,
    so deploy is not affected.
  - The fix is to judge 1b per commit on the pull request too, gathering
    each commit's files the way the range mode already does. That needs
    agent-guard.mjs and agent-boundary.yml and is not in this patch.
  - Decide whether to apply this patch before that fix exists.
- Paths with no lane are refused.
  - The manifest's comment lists the paths no role may edit: the
    composition roots under backend/crates/apps/*/src, backend/Cargo.lock,
    data/ and .github/rulesets/.
  - Once the switch is on, an agent commit touching one of them is
    refused. The same is true of a new file not yet in its lane's owns: add
    it to the manifest first.
- Overlaps are ordered by merge order.
  - Shared files are ordered by depends_on in merge order:
    - platform.rs: eight sessions' code lanes;
    - docs/adr/README.md: nine sessions' docs lanes;
    - the R12 register: all eleven sessions.
  - So `validate` prints 12 waves, and the widest has 6 lanes.
  - Those waves are not a run schedule. A max_concurrent_lanes cap set to
    "the largest wave" (L1b's ruling) would come out at 6 while eleven
    sessions run.
- docs/ops/runbooks/development-agent-controls.md:21 and ADR 0117 still
  name round-3.json as the round's plan. They are outside this patch's
  paths.

